.TH "SSOOSSHD-NSS" "8" "Aug 2026" "ssoosshd-nss" ""

.SH NAME
ssoosshd-nss-run - Run the daemon (the default with no subcommand).


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoosshd-nss run [flags] [args]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the userdb service. Under systemd the userdb socket comes from ssoosshd-nss.socket (socket activation); otherwise --listen binds one. SIGHUP re-reads the host files and the fleet key and clears the 401 latch, the offline backoff and the group name collisions and refused groups that status lists.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--cache-file\fP="/var/lib/ssoossh-nss/cache.db"
	the persistent cache's SQLite file

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for run

.PP
\fB--listen\fP=""
	bind the userdb socket at this path when not socket-activated (development and tests)

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="info"
	debug, info, warn or error


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--admin-socket\fP="/run/ssoossh-nss/admin.sock"
	the admin socket the CLI and the daemon share

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss.yaml"
	the daemon's configuration file

.PP
\fB--overrides\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss-overrides.yaml"
	the host override file


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBssoosshd-nss(8)\fP


